On the first glance its a nice space shooter with cool weapons. Unfortunately after you play for a while you find out its extremly simplistic and boring.
- once you get past tutorial you get a cycle of missions: kill 10 aliens, kill 10 pirates, destroy some blob or elite, deliver package to next system;
- ship progression is simplistic as every next ship has stats at 150% of the previous one. There is no choice of what you want and your only decision is if you want to upgrade or wait for next one for cash efficiency;

- actually you only rarely change weapons once you get something you like, since most modes are pretty situational and eveolving your main weapon is actually risky;
All in all its not a bad concept, but for now its more of a demo then a full game.

if you're looking for a hard super meat boy-like game with decent tracks (some are pretty good) and colorful, well-drawn levels backgrounds , you can give rush bros a try ,
although it has one of the worst things for a platforming game - laggy controls , it still manages to be challenging enough and dare i say satisfying once you master a level and finish it in a new record triggering that achievement notification (managed to get 21 achivements through 3 days for playfire rewards, if i play it more i'm sure i can get at least +40) ,
give it a try if you're into rage, hard games , maybe not with the 10$ price tag so wait for a sale (in case you haven't grabbed it for free at GMG promotion)

The game is in fact not THAT bad. One only needs to understand that it isn't a "real" Dead Island sequel nor Dying Light-type game. It is somewhat different thing and it can be enjoyable even if it lacks the complexity and depth of these titles. There is no real open world, only a feigned one. As in some older games, you cannot enter every area at first and you need to return to some places later (but I don't consider this a fault).
CONS:
- too expensive at 20 euros  (and it was horrendously expensive earlier), but when on a 50% sale, I think it's worth the money;
- the character cannot jump nor walk over high ledges (it means you cannot fall over ledges, but hey, being not able to jump over a bench or table?);
- the character cannot stand up from the crawl when too close to obstacles, and it spoils many "silence-kill" opportunities;
- stupid old-console-like saving system;
- voice acting - too exaggerate as for my taste, at least in the recordings you found during the gameplay.
PROS (IMHO):
- very nice, comic-style graphics (event if some textures ARE ugly);
- funny ideas as visible words depicting sounds (consistent with the comic-style look);
- a deeper insight into the original Dead Island incident (not too original though);
- good music and sound;
- nice character design;
- just right difficulty (I hate games that are too hard, I don't have the time for many repeated attempts, I have my job and family to care for ;) ).

Shmup which focuses less on avoiding bullets and more on "firepower gathering" if you will. As a casual player, I prefer this over so called "bullet hell" shmups. So, yeah, short review:
Pros:
+artstyle (old, but still appealing in some way);
+focuses on weapon-combining. Lots of different combos and ships;
+tracks are very well made;
+explosions;
+B-movie-type story;
Cons:
-it is hard to recognise what is in front of the ship and what object are in the background;
-level are too long (and there are no in-game ability to speed up levels). At later playthroughs (7 and later) there are moments, when just pressing one button and waiting for level to end. Pretty stupid game design and me for playing this beyond PL4;
-balance at later playthroughs made my eyeroll - enemy damage output increases slightly, but their collision damage increases significantly, so from those 43 levels only several challenged me (level without my ship). Oh, but you could say, KM, just play it without best weapons, to those peolpe I say without powerful gear this game is as lame as Borderlands playthrough with level 1 weapons.
-weapon variety is impressive, BUT at the end, only few most effective stay in play - Tsunami "beyblade" Beta (great idea,  aggressive playstyle/close distance required), Chronic Whatever (pierces every object in the game) and Armagedonattor (big a** blast, relatively long cooldown).
Btw, top negative comments give some really good points about the game, I agree with most of them, however, if you are like me - "filthy casual" - and have some cash to burn, I recommend you JnGGold. I advise playing it for up to 3 playthroughs and move on. Bought it on sale, did not regret.
And don't search for "Punisher". Just. Don't.

