Pros:
1) gameplay is fun and challenging;
2) many unique characters to choose from and all are viable if you play to their style;
3) The game is beautiful;
4) teamwork can be very satisfying;
5) although not perfect, the classes seem balanced.
Cons:
1) matchmaking can fail sometimes;
2) story mode can be painful if you don't like being forced to use a class you don't like.
3) combos and timing can feel inconsistent.
The biggest complaint I have read about the game is the P2P connection but this has not been my experience. My connections have been overwhelmingly positive. There has been a random occasion or two that lag degraded my experience but this has been rare. As I read the reviews complaining about the P2P and when I compare it to my experience, I feel as if those people are simply complaining to just complain. However, there are little things that I see that may be the result of P2P. The only significant one is the counter to guard break. It is so easy to grab someone but to counter it is incredibly difficult to execute. I have see YouTube videos of people easily doing in 1v1 or 2v2 but it is less so for me. I can easily do it against the AI but PvP it is hard. It may be that I suck or it may be the slight delay.
The next common complaint about the game I have read is that the classes are unbalanced under the reasoning that I play x-class and I can never beat y-class. I strongly oppose this argument. I love that one class is inherently weak to another and visa-versa. I have played long hours in Dark Souls/Demon's Souls/Bloodborne and I am use to equipping gear to suit your playstyle but it comes with a price. Regardless of the builds weaknesses if you play smart and patient then you can overcome any opponent. The same holds true to For Honor; you need to understand your class, know which battles you have the advantage, know when you are outmatched, and do what is needed to win.
The third complaint I have read is that this game is a button-smasher. IT IS NOT. I am not that good but I will crush anyone coming at me smashing buttons. There are counters for everything and if you are not willing to take the time to learn and master your build's combos then you will have a miserable experience once the rest of the community grows with experience. However, if two inexperienced individuals battle each other then the game very much may feel like a button-smashing game but in reality you simply don't know what you are doing.
